@startuml task-states
' The only legal task transitions. Anything else is a bug.

title Task status transitions

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #999999
}

[*] --> pending : task created by the API,\nthe scheduler, or a retry

pending --> running : worker wins the atomic claim\n(UPDATE ... WHERE status='pending')
running --> success : container exits 0
running --> failed : container fails **and**\nretry_count < max_retries
running --> final_failed : container fails **and**\nretries are exhausted
running --> pending : lock expired —\nthe scheduler reclaimed it

failed --> [*] : a new task carries retry_count + 1
success --> [*]
final_failed --> [*] : POST /tasks/{id}/retry\ncreates a fresh task

note right of pending
  A message sits in exactly one queue:
  normal (on demand or dependency),
  scheduled (cron), or retry.
end note

note right of running
  locked_by / locked_until are held by one
  worker and refreshed by its heartbeat.
  If that worker dies, the lock expires and
  recover_orphans returns the task to pending.
end note

note bottom of failed
  "failed" is not terminal — it records one
  attempt. "final_failed" is where a job
  actually gave up.
end note
@enduml
